WEBVTT

00:00:04.010 --> 00:00:06.840
Misumaru Yurika, captain of the Nadesico, age twenty.

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:10.480
Few expected her to be so committed a captain, but thanks to her,

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:16.230
the high mobility battleship Nadesico headed for Mars as a civilian vessel.

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:18.770
Oh well, whatever.

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:58.660
Barrier Satellites for Barrier System
First Defensive Line

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:05.710
The First Defensive Line prevents the infiltration of Jovian forces.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:09.030
The Big Barrier, created by nuclear fusion powered satellites,

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:12.520
works both ways and is an obstacle in the Nadesico's attempt to leave Earth.

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:15.100
I sure wouldn't want to die in a place like this.

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:16.020
No, I mean it.

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:20.710
A "Goodbye" That Came Too Soon!

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:24.690
We can't look over the existence of the Battleship Nadesico anymore.

00:02:24.690 --> 00:02:27.610
UEAF HQ

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:28.190
Command HQ - Main Conference Hall

00:02:28.190 --> 00:02:31.790
The period of wars between nations is on hold.

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:34.770
We must fight against unknown hostile forces from beyond Jupiter.

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:36.950
UEAF Chief Commander

00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:37.470
America's representative

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:38.890
The Nadesico is, however, going to have her own way.

00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:40.290
China's representative

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:41.700
Ociania Community's representative

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:46.140
Such action might ruin the peace of the whole Earth.

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:50.370
Chief Commander, incoming emergency by way of the White House.

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:51.370
What?

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:53.890
Eh, from the Nadesico, sir.

00:02:55.630 --> 00:02:58.070
Happy New Year!

00:02:58.810 --> 00:02:58.840
India's representative

00:02:58.840 --> 00:02:59.640
Fujiyama!
India's representative

00:02:59.640 --> 00:02:59.800
I'll take over from here.

00:02:59.800 --> 00:02:59.980
India's representative

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:00.700
Geisha!

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:01.070
India's representative
I'll take over from here.

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:02.720
You seem to be a little stressed out.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.450
Oh, foreigners don't understand Japanese.

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:07.070
Charm is an important tool too.

00:03:07.070 --> 00:03:10.230
You should start by learning manners fit for a global age.

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:13.310
Oh, thank you for the greetings.

00:03:13.310 --> 00:03:14.910
Unfortunately, we have little time to talk.

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:20.510
We'd like to reach escape velocity from the Earth in three hours, but...

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:24.030
If you don't put the Big Barrier down for a moment,

00:03:24.030 --> 00:03:27.700
the Nadesico and the barrier satellites will be damaged.

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:33.030
Would you mind to put the Big Barrier down, please?

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:35.130
Disable the Big Barrier?

00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:37.640
Demanding thieves we have here. Enough of this!

00:03:37.640 --> 00:03:39.900
So? We'll break through the Barrier forcibly.

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:42.010
Well, this makes it clear now.

00:03:42.470 --> 00:03:44.320
The Nadesico is an enemy of the UEAF!

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:46.330
Oh, so?

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:47.910
I do hope this will remain civilized.

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:55.440
This matter is no longer confined to the Far Eastern Command.

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:58.040
There's no hope for order unless we sink the Nadesico!

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:02.210
But if we sink that ship, we will be losing the most advanced and powerful vessel we have.

00:04:02.210 --> 00:04:02.800
Tanaka Saburo
Far East Instructor

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:05.260
Over seventy percent of the crew are of Japanese nationality.

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:05.370
Tanaka Saburo
Far East Instructor

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:08.420
Admiral Misumaru, please give us some insight.

00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:10.180
Well...

00:04:10.590 --> 00:04:12.940
While she is my daughter,
I'm taken aback at the boldness of this woman.

00:04:13.590 --> 00:04:15.950
She looks far too amorous in that kimono.

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:20.410
Sixth defensive line

00:04:20.410 --> 00:04:21.930
UESF within the Pacific Coastal Region are in pursuit.

00:04:21.930 --> 00:04:24.850
Fifth defensive line

00:04:24.850 --> 00:04:25.490
UEAF Command HQ

00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:28.650
Good, we should be able to intercept before she reaches the stratosphere.

00:04:28.890 --> 00:04:30.810
Well, actually...

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:35.280
It's been awhile since we had such a large, organized military deployment,

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:40.190
so the Jovian forces have responded, resulting in a series of fierce battles.

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:44.510
Nadesico, I'll never forgive you for this!

00:04:45.030 --> 00:04:46.370
Get me the Third Defensive Line!

00:04:46.370 --> 00:04:46.380
Forth defensive line
Get me the Third Defensive Line!

00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:49.370
Forth defensive line

00:04:49.610 --> 00:04:52.260
Gekigan Punch!

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:55.350
What?!

00:04:57.700 --> 00:04:58.800
Damn!

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:01.640
Gekigan Punch is made with Gekiganium Alloy!

00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:04.860
That was rather entertaining, Earthlings.

00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:07.050
But this is the end!

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:12.170
Damn, it's the UEAF again.

00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:14.600
Come on, Yurika, this is just getting interesting!

00:05:14.990 --> 00:05:16.030
There's nothing she can do.

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:20.270
The Distortion Field is a defense against Jovian Gravity Blasts.

00:05:20.270 --> 00:05:24.120
It's only natural that it won't be as effective against physical attacks.

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:25.620
You understand now?

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:27.420
Aren't you supposed to be standing by?

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:30.030
You still don't get it, do you?

00:05:30.690 --> 00:05:34.050
How can robots shoot down all incoming missiles?!

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:37.600
Robots are truly meant for hand to hand combat against other robots!

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:42.460
That means I'll be going into action when we hit the Third Defensive Line!

00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:47.760
This time no cook is going to upstage me!

00:05:48.190 --> 00:05:49.520
Do what you want.

00:05:51.020 --> 00:05:52.820
All right then!

00:05:52.820 --> 00:05:53.270
I'll make sure the Nadesico reaches space no matter what happens!

00:05:53.270 --> 00:05:53.820
Damn it!

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:54.610
I'll make sure the Nadesico reaches space no matter what happens!

00:05:54.610 --> 00:05:55.670
We never lose!

00:05:55.670 --> 00:05:56.760
I'll make sure the Nadesico reaches space no matter what happens!

00:05:56.760 --> 00:05:58.030
Gekiganger is Invincible!

00:05:58.030 --> 00:05:59.360
If you get in my way,

00:05:59.360 --> 00:06:00.580
I won't show you what comes after episode twenty-six.

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:03.580
Isn't episode twenty-six the last episode?

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:04.970
Baka!

00:06:04.970 --> 00:06:08.100
They changed the time slot, and went on for another season.

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:10.070
Please, please, you have to let me watch them!

00:06:11.740 --> 00:06:15.420
In that case, I want you to swear that you will never pilot my robot again!

00:06:16.470 --> 00:06:19.660
Currently, the Earth is shielded by seven separate lines of defense.

00:06:20.390 --> 00:06:23.880
We will need to defeat each one in reverse order.

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:26.900
We have already gone beyond the range of the SCRAM-2 jet fighters.

00:06:27.140 --> 00:06:29.150
The airborne fleet is engaged in battle with the Battas.

00:06:29.830 --> 00:06:32.190
These two have been effectively neutralized,

00:06:32.190 --> 00:06:35.600
and we are now under attack by missiles launched from the ground.

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:37.990
In other words we are currently breaching the Fourth Defensive Line.

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:40.000
This is so tedious.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:42.560
Why can't we just blast our way into space?

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:44.410
True, but unfortunately we can't do that.

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:48.980
To leave Earth's gravity, we need an escape velocity of 11 .2 km/sec.

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:56.380
We must bring the Phase Transition Engine into the red zone in order for the Nadesico to reach that velocity.

00:06:57.010 --> 00:07:02.970
Since the engine obtains energy by phasing through vacuum,

00:07:02.970 --> 00:07:03.280
Nadesico - Engine Room

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:06.890
for peak performance, we must be at higher altitudes with better vacuum.

00:07:07.240 --> 00:07:10.000
Effective phase transition cannot take place below an altitude of 20,000km.

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:12.150
But before we reach that altitude,

00:07:12.150 --> 00:07:15.210
we will need to get past the Third and Second Defensive Lines.

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:19.670
The Distortion Field seems to have weakened again.

00:07:20.420 --> 00:07:22.120
Ouch, ouch, ouch!

00:07:23.570 --> 00:07:25.010
May I suggest that you change your attire?

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:27.790
Yes, I think I will!

00:07:28.490 --> 00:07:29.700
But before that...

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:34.680
Because of what happed before, I haven't been coming here.

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:36.170
Today, for sure!

00:07:37.310 --> 00:07:39.230
Akito!

00:07:39.230 --> 00:07:41.020
JOE!

00:07:43.740 --> 00:07:45.610
What is it, Akito?

00:07:47.380 --> 00:07:49.040
What are you two doing alone in here?

00:07:49.040 --> 00:07:50.470
My dear Joe has...

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:52.700
Also Gekiganger has...

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:54.330
Died!

00:07:55.730 --> 00:07:57.550
You get it! You get it!

00:07:57.850 --> 00:07:59.620
You understand what's in this too!

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:01.340
You understand this too!

00:08:02.140 --> 00:08:07.150
Umitsubame Joe's sacrifice drove General Masaka's attack back.

00:08:07.150 --> 00:08:11.730
But now Gekiganger 3 is hurt and is missing a pilot.

00:08:11.730 --> 00:08:13.890
JOE...!

00:08:13.890 --> 00:08:15.890
Will they be able to recover from this loss?

00:08:16.230 --> 00:08:16.240
You have to get back up, Gekiganger! The future is at stake!

00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:20.760
That is the way a man should go, man. Dying in battle, sacrificing one's self for the sake of friends!

00:08:21.070 --> 00:08:22.700
Thank you! Thank you!

00:08:22.700 --> 00:08:24.930
For showing something this good to me!

00:08:27.450 --> 00:08:29.660
I'm much better than this stuff.

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:33.630
How long do you think you'll be able to get away with this imprisonment?

00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:36.360
This treatment clearly goes against all international POW conventions!

00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:40.730
Keep it up, and I'll customize your asses but leave your brain to enjoy it.

00:08:40.730 --> 00:08:42.780
Keep still for awhile, damn it!

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:45.360
How is it?

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:46.450
This is too easy.

00:08:47.030 --> 00:08:49.870
Using rope in this day and age, they really are amateurs.

00:08:50.360 --> 00:08:54.290
I'm not in the mood to accompany the Nadesico into space.

00:08:55.390 --> 00:08:57.620
We'll make our escape when fighting breaks out.

00:08:59.190 --> 00:08:59.950
Third Defensive Line

00:08:59.950 --> 00:09:01.130
You must listen to me, Aoi-kun.

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:03.810
You're a junior officer with a career ahead of you.

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:06.180
Stopping the Nadesico is my mission!

00:09:06.180 --> 00:09:07.760
But to undergo nano-machine treatment...

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:10.930
He's right. There's no reason why you need to have this done.

00:09:11.470 --> 00:09:15.090
This is no big deal. Anyone that becomes a pilot goes through this.

00:09:15.090 --> 00:09:17.690
Note: IFS = Image Feedback System
Without this, you can't use the IFS.

00:09:18.060 --> 00:09:20.270
I've completely given up on Yurika.

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:21.910
So, please?!

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:22.310
Give me that!

00:09:34.450 --> 00:09:36.580
Stop squandering precious time! Move it!

00:09:36.940 --> 00:09:40.810
You'll be able to control the Delphinium as if it were part of you.

00:09:40.810 --> 00:09:43.470
The external fuel tanks will give you at least one full hour of flight time.

00:09:44.090 --> 00:09:46.700
As long as you maintain a proper thrust vector, you won't fall.

00:09:47.080 --> 00:09:49.140
Please make it back safely.

00:09:49.450 --> 00:09:50.390
Thanks for everything.

00:09:51.060 --> 00:09:52.520
Then, good luck!

00:09:53.690 --> 00:09:54.390
Goodbye.

00:10:11.350 --> 00:10:12.450
Destination...

00:10:13.220 --> 00:10:14.720
High mobility battleship Nadesico!

00:10:20.790 --> 00:10:21.920
All right!

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:25.000
Get out my way! Move it, move it!

00:10:25.330 --> 00:10:25.700
This close to the Earth,
Electromagnetic conditions couldn't be worse.

00:10:25.700 --> 00:10:26.730
I'll crush you if you get in the way!

00:10:26.730 --> 00:10:27.210
Raise the broadcast power to maximum.
This close to the Earth,

00:10:27.210 --> 00:10:28.560
Nadesico's engine won't reach the red zone.

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:29.120
I'll crush you if you get in the way!

00:10:29.120 --> 00:10:29.140
Pilots may be able to communicate.

00:10:29.140 --> 00:10:30.970
I, Daigoji Gai-sama!
Nadesico's engine won't reach the red zone.

00:10:30.970 --> 00:10:30.990
Don't make me repeat.
Pilots may be able to communicate.

00:10:30.990 --> 00:10:31.690
I, Daigoji Gai-sama!
Don't make me repeat.

00:10:31.690 --> 00:10:31.820
Any questions?

00:10:31.820 --> 00:10:32.240
Hi, hi. Hi, hi!
Don't make me repeat.

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:33.010
Getting too far away outside the range,
Any questions?

00:10:33.010 --> 00:10:34.310
I will handle the third defense line!
Getting too far away outside the range,

00:10:34.310 --> 00:10:35.070
you won't be able to move.

00:10:35.070 --> 00:10:35.890
Don't have one?

00:10:35.890 --> 00:10:36.130
you won't be able to move.
I will handle the third defense line!

00:10:36.130 --> 00:10:36.930
Hey, listen!
I will handle the third defense line!

00:10:37.270 --> 00:10:37.440
With these hands we will reclaim it! Let's go, Gekiganger 3!

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:38.640
Damn it!

00:10:38.640 --> 00:10:40.430
He's not listening to a word I'm saying.
With these hands we will reclaim it! Let's go, Gekiganger 3!

00:10:40.430 --> 00:10:41.990
Disconnect the line from the bridge.

00:10:41.990 --> 00:10:44.940
All right, Professor. Lower the laboratory force field!

00:10:45.210 --> 00:10:45.950
That's all.

00:10:46.100 --> 00:10:47.660
So, where is Tenkawa?

00:10:47.660 --> 00:10:48.910
Him?

00:10:49.070 --> 00:10:49.860
JOE!

00:10:50.090 --> 00:10:50.220
I left him in his room crying his heart out.

00:10:50.220 --> 00:10:52.220
You must stand up!

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:53.860
Oh, well...

00:10:54.600 --> 00:10:58.580
Delphiniums of the Third Defensive Line approaching, 30 degrees port.

00:10:58.580 --> 00:11:01.020
Elevation 60 degrees, distance 8,000 meters.

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:05.210
Let's Gekiga-in...

00:11:05.580 --> 00:11:07.630
Hello! Here they come!

00:11:07.750 --> 00:11:09.800
All coming in a mass!

00:11:15.680 --> 00:11:16.230
Here I go!

00:11:16.490 --> 00:11:19.150
How long until we have max thrust from the Phase Transition Engine?

00:11:19.330 --> 00:11:21.810
Another 19,750km.

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:23.110
What do we do?

00:11:23.730 --> 00:11:24.370
Let's do it.

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:25.780
That's what I was waiting for!

00:11:26.100 --> 00:11:29.110
I'll show you how real heroes fight their battles!

00:11:30.920 --> 00:11:32.280
To-raaa!

00:11:32.820 --> 00:11:33.320
Attack!

00:11:38.680 --> 00:11:39.550
That idiot!

00:11:39.550 --> 00:11:40.710
It's okay, okay!

00:11:48.910 --> 00:11:50.790
All right, here they come after me!

00:11:51.240 --> 00:11:52.350
Okay, Uribatake!

00:11:53.070 --> 00:11:55.010
Time for you to launch the Space Gangar heavy armaments module!

00:11:57.710 --> 00:11:59.370
Yamada-san's requesting something.

00:11:59.370 --> 00:12:02.370
If he's not willing to listen to anything we say, just leave it.

00:12:02.370 --> 00:12:05.550
Like I said, launch the Space Gangar heavy armaments module.

00:12:05.550 --> 00:12:07.990
I have no idea what a space something or astro whatever is.

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:10.030
This ship doesn't have this Gangar thing you keep talking about.

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:12.540
Maybe he's talking about the B module for unit one?

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:13.810
Oh yeah, that's it!

00:12:14.670 --> 00:12:15.290
All right...

00:12:15.500 --> 00:12:17.280
Here it comes. Make sure to catch it.

00:12:18.950 --> 00:12:19.460
This is perfect.

00:12:20.150 --> 00:12:22.970
I rush down below them, and lure them in.

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:25.130
The enemy thinks I have no weapons.

00:12:25.180 --> 00:12:28.010
But then I combine with the heavy armaments module in mid-air!

00:12:28.070 --> 00:12:29.630
And crush them all in one sweep!

00:12:29.740 --> 00:12:32.390
I call this the "Gangar Cross Operation!"

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:34.960
There you are!

00:12:35.420 --> 00:12:36.890
Here it comes!

00:12:37.630 --> 00:12:38.600
Let's..

00:12:38.600 --> 00:12:40.140
Gangar Cross!

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:44.820
Ano, might it be that your plan failed?

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:46.630
Hell no!

00:12:46.630 --> 00:12:48.280
Mind over matter!

00:12:48.280 --> 00:12:53.320
Gai Super Napalm!

00:12:56.890 --> 00:12:58.510
This'll work out just fine!

00:13:00.580 --> 00:13:02.330
Yamada-san's completely surrounded.

00:13:03.590 --> 00:13:04.500
We're counting on you, Tenkawa.

00:13:04.540 --> 00:13:06.410
Jeez, what is he doing?

00:13:11.590 --> 00:13:13.340
Yurika, this is your last chance.

00:13:13.760 --> 00:13:14.590
Turn the Nadesico around!

00:13:15.320 --> 00:13:16.280
Jun-kun!

00:13:16.280 --> 00:13:18.010
Your actions violate our contract.

00:13:18.540 --> 00:13:19.610
Yurika...

00:13:19.610 --> 00:13:21.420
I will take you back, even by force .

00:13:21.750 --> 00:13:25.180
If you resist, the Nadesico will face the wrath of the Third Defensive Line.

00:13:25.600 --> 00:13:26.520
Got ya!

00:13:27.540 --> 00:13:27.930
What?!

00:13:29.900 --> 00:13:31.400
I don't want to fight you.

00:13:31.750 --> 00:13:34.950
19,650 km until maximum engine thrust.

00:13:35.550 --> 00:13:36.950
What will it be, Captain?

00:13:38.020 --> 00:13:40.860
Sorry, Jun-kun. I can't leave my post.

00:13:42.320 --> 00:13:44.420
You mean to fight?

00:13:44.490 --> 00:13:46.270
This is where I belong.

00:13:46.270 --> 00:13:49.370
Here I'm not the admiral's eldest daughter, not my father's daughter.

00:13:50.220 --> 00:13:53.220
This is the only place where I can be my true self.

00:13:56.790 --> 00:13:57.800
As I thought.

00:13:58.560 --> 00:13:59.550
Is he that important?

00:14:03.070 --> 00:14:05.070
All right, Yurika.

00:14:05.700 --> 00:14:07.810
Then I'll start with demolishing this robot!

00:14:07.970 --> 00:14:09.670
Damn it, let me go!

00:14:13.280 --> 00:14:14.280
Stop it!

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:16.990
Akito!

00:14:17.240 --> 00:14:18.400
Stop this crap!

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:21.400
We were friends just hours ago!

00:14:22.520 --> 00:14:24.310
If you are so intent on blocking my path,

00:14:25.240 --> 00:14:27.410
then fight me, Tenkawa Akito!

00:14:28.140 --> 00:14:29.630
One on one.

00:14:29.630 --> 00:14:32.360
If I lose, I will have the other Delphiniums withdraw.

00:14:32.730 --> 00:14:33.560
How can he?!

00:14:35.610 --> 00:14:37.260
It's not a bad deal.

00:14:37.590 --> 00:14:38.550
Do it, Akito!

00:14:38.550 --> 00:14:40.470
That's how a real man would fight!

00:14:40.470 --> 00:14:41.680
I won't be part of such insanity!

00:14:41.980 --> 00:14:42.820
Here I come!

00:14:43.450 --> 00:14:44.850
Tenkawa Akito!

00:14:47.230 --> 00:14:48.100
Stop it!

00:14:48.600 --> 00:14:50.440
I have no intention of fighting you!

00:14:51.050 --> 00:14:52.160
Lieutenant!

00:14:52.160 --> 00:14:53.400
Oh no, you don't.

00:14:53.400 --> 00:14:54.690
I'm your opponent.

00:14:55.280 --> 00:14:58.870
Interrupting men engaged in mortal combat is nothing short of rude!

00:15:01.560 --> 00:15:03.220
We have now breached the Third Defensive Line.

00:15:03.220 --> 00:15:07.240
19,550 km until maximum engine thrust.

00:15:08.680 --> 00:15:11.880
Phase Transition Engine power, 50%. Vessel velocity steadily increasing!

00:15:12.220 --> 00:15:14.920
I wonder why Jun-kun is so hung up on Akito?

00:15:16.360 --> 00:15:18.440
Why, Captain, I'm sure you know.

00:15:18.440 --> 00:15:19.810
It's all about a man's passion.

00:15:19.810 --> 00:15:20.390
What?

00:15:20.460 --> 00:15:22.300
Because Aoi-san is the captain's...

00:15:22.730 --> 00:15:23.970
My best friend.

00:15:25.580 --> 00:15:28.390
19, 400km until maximum engine thrust.

00:15:28.560 --> 00:15:30.450
Wait! Wait! Wait a minute!

00:15:30.450 --> 00:15:32.270
You're getting this all wrong!

00:15:32.270 --> 00:15:34.640
I have nothing to do with Yurika!

00:15:34.640 --> 00:15:35.810
I don't believe you!

00:15:35.810 --> 00:15:37.900
Besides this has nothing to do with such private affairs!

00:15:38.260 --> 00:15:39.950
Then, why?

00:15:39.950 --> 00:15:42.620
Are you that desperate to fight a war?!

00:15:43.790 --> 00:15:46.980
Ever since I was a child, I wanted to help protect the Earth.

00:15:46.980 --> 00:15:50.900
And I believe that the UESF is the place I can realize those dreams!

00:15:50.900 --> 00:15:52.180
I believed in the same thing.

00:15:52.540 --> 00:15:55.920
If you have faith, you can make a difference, and be a hero, someday.

00:15:56.380 --> 00:15:57.840
I blindly followed my goal.

00:15:59.550 --> 00:16:00.590
But I couldn't make it.

00:16:00.810 --> 00:16:01.760
I'm different!

00:16:01.980 --> 00:16:04.430
19,000 km until maximum engine thrust.

00:16:04.760 --> 00:16:07.230
We are about to enter the effective range of the Second Defensive Line.

00:16:08.640 --> 00:16:11.060
Second Defensive Line

00:16:12.270 --> 00:16:14.020
I will protect the Earth through my efforts!

00:16:14.360 --> 00:16:15.690
I will make sure that what is just is done!

00:16:16.170 --> 00:16:18.740
Pride and righteousness over personal freedom.

00:16:19.100 --> 00:16:20.150
Never to forget that!

00:16:21.520 --> 00:16:26.200
Bastard!

00:16:28.230 --> 00:16:29.780
You're starting to impress me, Akito!

00:16:30.230 --> 00:16:33.210
A fight between real men has got to be like this!

00:16:34.810 --> 00:16:35.620
What do you think you're doing?

00:16:36.000 --> 00:16:37.460
I've heard enough!

00:16:37.890 --> 00:16:43.220
Do you want to be a hero who bashes people's heads to win your true love?

00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:49.550
Because she is my true love, I can't watch her become Earth's enemy!

00:16:49.980 --> 00:16:51.230
Damn!

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:53.400
The armed satellites have the Nadesico in range!

00:16:53.750 --> 00:16:57.120
15,000 km until maximum engine thrust.

00:16:57.120 --> 00:16:59.320
If the missiles come now, we won't be able to evade them.

00:17:04.860 --> 00:17:05.930
What's going on?

00:17:06.290 --> 00:17:07.660
I can't move.

00:17:07.660 --> 00:17:09.070
I've run out of energy as well.

00:17:09.560 --> 00:17:12.170
The two Aestivalis are beyond the maximum energy transfer distance.

00:17:12.410 --> 00:17:15.470
Missiles from armed satellites are approaching from three directions.

00:17:15.470 --> 00:17:18.090
10,000 km until maximum engine thrust.

00:17:19.850 --> 00:17:22.290
Engine accelerating smoothly!

00:17:22.290 --> 00:17:23.670
Missiles approaching fast!

00:17:28.360 --> 00:17:29.930
That idiot is going to block the missiles with his body!

00:17:30.160 --> 00:17:30.600
Jun!

00:17:30.750 --> 00:17:32.020
Stop!

00:17:32.290 --> 00:17:33.350
Yeah,

00:17:33.350 --> 00:17:34.380
I've always known

00:17:34.940 --> 00:17:37.180
I could never be a real hero.

00:17:38.270 --> 00:17:40.010
The military is only interested in fighting wars.

00:17:40.460 --> 00:17:42.310
After all, what is justice?!

00:17:44.970 --> 00:17:48.930
Yurika, this might have been what I was wishing for from the beginning.

00:17:49.770 --> 00:17:51.100
If it for protecting you...

00:17:51.820 --> 00:17:53.630
This place is where I belonged to.

00:17:55.960 --> 00:17:58.290
For crying out loud, stop being such a troublemaker!

00:17:58.820 --> 00:18:00.100
I thought you were immobilized?

00:18:00.480 --> 00:18:02.270
The Nadesico caught up to us.

00:18:02.660 --> 00:18:06.050
300 km until maximum engine thrust.

00:18:06.210 --> 00:18:06.800
Here she comes!

00:18:06.800 --> 00:18:07.160
250...

00:18:07.160 --> 00:18:08.640
The engine's really starting to cook!

00:18:08.640 --> 00:18:08.840
200...

00:18:08.840 --> 00:18:10.310
Distortion field maximum strength!

00:18:10.310 --> 00:18:10.930
150...

00:18:10.930 --> 00:18:10.980
Distortion field maximum strength!

00:18:10.980 --> 00:18:12.130
Everyone prepare for breaching the Barrier.

00:18:12.130 --> 00:18:12.500
100

00:18:12.500 --> 00:18:13.680
Everyone prepare for breaching the Barrier.

00:18:13.910 --> 00:18:14.530
50...

00:18:16.430 --> 00:18:18.030
Maximum engine thrust.

00:18:29.670 --> 00:18:31.260
You never know.

00:18:31.260 --> 00:18:34.210
We may still become heroes.

00:18:34.630 --> 00:18:36.960
Someone needs to baby-sit Yurika.

00:18:38.420 --> 00:18:41.320
You're telling me that I'm free to do that on the Nadesico?

00:18:41.320 --> 00:18:42.480
Something like that.

00:18:42.990 --> 00:18:45.480
I was born a hero.

00:18:45.970 --> 00:18:46.800
Yeah, sure.

00:18:47.240 --> 00:18:48.850
Don't let them breach the Barrier!

00:18:48.850 --> 00:18:50.470
I don't care if the nuclear power plants meltdown!

00:19:10.530 --> 00:19:11.990
And so...

00:19:12.390 --> 00:19:18.240
The Earth must be feeling the effects of the nuclear plant shutdowns in the form of a massive blackout.

00:19:18.240 --> 00:19:20.370
Serves them right though.

00:19:20.820 --> 00:19:21.710
Yurika, I'm sorry.

00:19:21.970 --> 00:19:23.630
You have nothing to apologize for.

00:19:23.960 --> 00:19:27.790
As my best friend, you were worried about me, right?

00:19:28.090 --> 00:19:29.480
Well, actually...

00:19:29.480 --> 00:19:33.630
Oh, Akito, thank you for not hurting my very best friend!

00:19:33.630 --> 00:19:35.390
Well you know,

00:19:35.390 --> 00:19:37.910
I didn't save him just because he was your friend!

00:19:37.910 --> 00:19:39.810
Oh come on, all of you!

00:19:39.810 --> 00:19:42.190
Things are bound to get better as long as you're alive.

00:19:42.190 --> 00:19:45.110
Just make sure not to die looking better than me, all right?

00:19:45.110 --> 00:19:46.320
What's that?

00:19:46.320 --> 00:19:47.450
Oh, this? This?

00:19:48.940 --> 00:19:50.270
Those are Gekigan stickers!

00:19:50.270 --> 00:19:53.870
I took care of six bogeys, man. I have to put these up on my Space Gangar.

00:19:54.640 --> 00:19:56.740
Ken, finish him off!

00:19:56.740 --> 00:19:58.330
Stop, Joe!

00:19:58.760 --> 00:20:01.340
But, Joe, what about you?

00:20:01.340 --> 00:20:02.750
JOE...!

00:20:05.100 --> 00:20:06.590
Don't worry about me.

00:20:08.370 --> 00:20:10.760
If we let them get away now, they'll demolish Tokyo!

00:20:12.020 --> 00:20:13.180
Do it, Ken!

00:20:14.420 --> 00:20:15.610
Ken!

00:20:15.610 --> 00:20:17.100
Gekigan Flare, now!

00:20:18.030 --> 00:20:21.460
Let me see now. I wonder where I should put them?

00:20:21.460 --> 00:20:21.770
Ah!

00:20:23.670 --> 00:20:24.410
Eh?

00:20:24.410 --> 00:20:25.360
Hey, you!

00:20:28.730 --> 00:20:30.580
Gekigan Flare!

00:20:34.630 --> 00:20:36.610
I'm sorry, Nanako-san.

00:20:36.610 --> 00:20:39.730
Looks like I won't be able to take you to the beach.

00:21:29.610 --> 00:21:40.560
looking nobody else's but "my" future

00:21:46.500 --> 00:21:50.860
Tenkawa Akito flies his Aestivalis through the ever-expansive universe!

00:21:50.860 --> 00:21:53.460
Watch me, friend. I'll get them all!

00:21:53.460 --> 00:21:56.950
Do space witches await courageous men that venture into the void?

00:21:57.270 --> 00:21:59.950
With a script written by Nadehisa Arakawa of Blue Seed fame,

00:22:00.220 --> 00:22:04.040
the romance-comedy factor shoots up 150% according to our testing.

00:22:04.040 --> 00:22:06.150
Next Martian Successor Nadesico:

00:22:06.150 --> 00:22:08.540
"Charmed by Sky Blue Space!"

00:22:08.620 --> 00:22:10.950
Let's watch it, everyone!
